# WASI is a *build-machine* toolchain, not a target one. Firefox compiles its
# RLBox-sandboxed libraries (graphite2, hunspell, ogg, expat, woff2) to
# wasm32 with the build host's clang against /usr/share/wasi-sysroot, then
# wasm2c turns the result into C that the *target* compiler builds. The
# sysroot only ever contains wasm32-wasip1/p2 objects and wasi-compiler-rt
# installs into the host clang's own resource dir, so there is no such thing
# as an aarch64 WASI package and none is needed -- these stay native.
wasi-compiler-rt crossnative make
wasi-libc crossnative make
wasi-libc++ crossnative make
# Host-side build tools a cross build still needs on the build machine.
